  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1971-p26.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Use mass points. Since \\(AF:FC=1:2,\\) assign masses \\(2\\) and \\(1\\) to \\(A\\) and \\(C,\\) so the mass at \\(F\\) is \\(3.\\) Because \\(G\\) is the midpoint of \\(BF,\\) the mass at \\(B\\) is also \\(3.\\) Therefore \\[ BE:EC=m_C:m_B=1:3. \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Assign endpoint masses so that \\(AF:FC=1:2\\)",
        "The midpoint condition makes the masses at \\(B\\) and \\(F\\) equal"
      ],
